## Course Pricing & What to Bring:

The **First Step Pistol Orientation** at Live Fire Instruction is a 3-hour express beginner firearms training course held at the **NRA National Firearms Museum Range in Fairfax, Virginia**. Taught by NRA-certified instructors, this beginner-friendly program provides a relaxed, no-pressure environment to learn the essential foundations of firearm safety and pistol operation.

* **Course Tuition:** $159.99 (Includes firearms usage and classroom materials)
* **Range & Ammo Fee:** $15–$35 paid directly to the range facility on class day.
* **What to Bring:** Government-issued photo ID, eye protection, and ear protection.

> **Safety Notice:** NO LIVE AMMUNITION IS PERMITTED IN THE CLASSROOM. All personal firearms brought to the facility must remain cased and completely unloaded until instructed on the live range.


---

## Also Consider These Related Courses

Once you have completed the First Step Pistol Orientation, Live Fire Instruction offers a full range of progressive courses to continue your firearm education:

- [NRA Basic Pistol Course in Fairfax, VA](/trainings/nra-basic-pistol-course-fairfax-va) — A comprehensive 6-hour course covering pistol mechanics, ammunition knowledge, and a full live-fire qualification
- [NRA Defensive Pistol Course](/trainings/nra-defensive-pistol-course) — Advanced defensive shooting skills for responsible concealed carriers
- [One-on-One Private Firearm Instruction](/private-shooting-lessons-northern-va) — Private, personalized instruction tailored to your specific goals at the NRA Range

